[size=5][b]psi_autocast: one-key psi casting[/b][/size]

Press one key: your character draws the psi amp, selects the discipline and casts it. No F-key cycling, no clicking, and no overload-bar timing (optional).

[line]
[size=4][b]Quick start[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into the folder with [b]SystemShock2Remastered.exe[/b].[/*]
[*]New Game → Mods → add [b]psi_autocast[/b] → Apply → start, then load your save and make a regular save.[/*]
[*]Build a macro in the [url=https://feygon.github.io/SS2PsiAutocast/Macro_Builder.html]Macro Builder[/url], or bind a ready-made script to a key.[/*]
[/list]

[line]
[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Works from any weapon.[/b] The key draws the amp, waits for it to come up, then casts.[/*]
[*][b]All 35 disciplines,[/b] each with a [b]quickfire[/b] script and a [b]conditional overload[/b] script.[/*]
[*][b]Conditional overload[/b] only overloads disciplines that benefit from it. (Many disciplines don't benefit from overloading.)[/*]
[*][b]Overload timing from the game's own data, adaptive to Psi Tier and Stats.[/b] Worked out on every cast from the tier and your current PSI.[/*]
[*][b]Chains:[/b] one key casts several disciplines in a row.[/*]
[*][b]Cancel key:[/b] stops a running macro.[/*]
[*][b]Psi hypos and weapon switching[/b] inside a macro.[/*]
[*][b]Console feedback:[/b] every cast reports its tier, PSI, overload zone and decision.[/*]
[/list]

[line]
[size=4][b]Macro Builder[/b][/size]
Open [b]psi\Macro_Builder.html[/b] from the download (it works offline), or use the [url=https://feygon.github.io/SS2PsiAutocast/Macro_Builder.html]online copy[/url].
[list]
[*][b]Settings first:[/b] auto psi hypo, and how long to wait for the amp to come up.[/*]
[*][b]Steps:[/b] add casts in order, each quickfire or conditional overload. A psi hypo can go anywhere.[/*]
[*][b]Finish with a weapon switch:[/b] back to the weapon you held before the macro drew the amp, or to any weapon by name.[/*]
[*][b]Output:[/b] the macro file (download or copy), the key binding line for user.bnd, and install steps.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Auto psi hypo:[/b] before each cast, the macro uses a psi hypo if your psi points are at or below your maximum minus what a hypo restores, so none is wasted. It reads your difficulty (30 on Easy, 20 otherwise) and the Pharmo-Friendly upgrade (+20%) itself.

[line]
[size=4][b]Action scripts[/b][/size]
One-line scripts in [i]psi\actions[/i] that you can bind to a key on their own:
[list]
[*][b]Cancel_Macro[/b]: stops any running macro. A cast that is mid-charge is released.[/*]
[*][b]Use_Psi_Hypo[/b]: uses a psi hypo.[/*]
[*][b]Switch_To_Previous_Weapon[/b]: switches back to the weapon you held when your last macro drew the amp.[/*]
[*][b]Switch_To_<Weapon>[/b]: switches to any weapon by name.[/*]
[/list]

[line]
[size=4][b]Binding a key[/b][/size]
Close the game, open [i]%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Nightdive Studios\System Shock 2 Remastered\user.bnd[/i] in Notepad, and add one line per key:
[code]bind g "run psi\T1_Projected_Cryokinesis_Quickfire.cmd"
bind j "run psi\T1_Projected_Cryokinesis.cmd"
bind keypad_plus "run psi\actions\Cancel_Macro.cmd"[/code]
The game rewrites user.bnd when it exits, so edits made while it's running are lost.

[spoiler][size=4][b]Install notes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The zip creates [i]mods\psi_autocast.kpf[/i] and a [i]psi[/i] folder of scripts.[/*]
[*]Each save stores its own mod list, so loading an older save directly won't enable the mod. Load it from inside a new game, then save.[/*]
[*][b]Don't use mod_apply mid-game:[/b] it can unload the level.[/*]
[/list][/spoiler]

[spoiler][size=4][b]Write your own macros[/b][/size]
Every script is a small text file built from shared parts in [i]psi\lib[/i], so you can make your own in Notepad:
[code]set psi_name T1_Projected_Cryokinesis
set psi_power 6
set psi_slot 0
set psi_benefits 1
run psi\lib\T1.cmd
run psi\lib\overload.cmd
run psi\lib\draw_cast.cmd[/code]
[list]
[*][b]T1.cmd to T5.cmd[/b] set the discipline's tier.[/*]
[*][b]quickfire.cmd[/b] or [b]overload.cmd[/b] chooses how it casts.[/*]
[*][b]draw_cast.cmd[/b] draws the amp if needed, then casts.[/*]
[/list]
Chains use the format the Macro Builder writes. [i]arm[/i] draws the amp, [i]6o[/i] is discipline 6 with conditional overload, [i]15q[/i] is discipline 15 quickfired, [i]w500[/i] waits 500 ms, [i]hypo[/i] uses a psi hypo, and [i]last[/i] switches back to your previous weapon:
[code]set psi_chain arm,6o,w500,hypo,w500,15q,w500,last
set psi_draw_ms 800
set psi_chain_gap_ms 500
set psi_auto_hypo 0
summon_obj PsiChain[/code]
Scripts are read fresh on every keypress, so you can edit them while the game is running. The readme lists every setting and every discipline number.[/spoiler]

[b]You can also have Claude write macros for you.[/b] Give Claude [i]psi\psi_autocast_MACROS_FOR_CLAUDE.md[/i] from the download and describe the macro you want.

[line]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]System Shock 2: 25th Anniversary Remaster on PC. Tested on the Epic version, game version 1.3.4984.[/*]
[*]Won't work on the classic 1999 version.[/*]
[*]Tested alongside the remaster's bundled mods (SCP beta 6, SHTUP, Four Hundred, patch_ext). Multiplayer is untested.[/*]
[/list]

